<title>JAPAN: Japan to spend Y200 mln for Argentine mine project.</title>
<headline>Japan to spend Y200 mln for Argentine mine project.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese government has agreed to spend 200 million yen over the next two years on a mine exploration project in eastern Argentina, the Metal Mining Agency of Japan said on Friday.</p>
<p>The project, financed by Japanese government aid, is aimed at finding copper, gold, lead and zinc in a 770,000,000 square metre area along the states of Larioja, San Juan and Mendoza near the border to Chile, an agency statement said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
